  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses exclusively on selecting the lottery with the higher probability of the maximum outcome (which is Lottery B with 25% vs. 20%). However, the individual chose Lottery A based on a trade-off between the higher potential gain (4000 vs. 3000) and the lower probability, indicating a different reasoning strategy (possibly expected value intuition or outcome prioritization). The individual did not prioritize the probability of the maximum outcome as the deciding factor. Instead, they weighed outcome size against probability difference. Therefore, the reasoning process described does not align with the decision reason. There is no indication that the individual selected based on maximizing the probability of the highest outcome; in fact, they chose the option with the lower such probability. The justification is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
